<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kashmir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kashmir is a mountainous region in the north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, famed for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawl">shawls</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> conquered it for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, and its revenues and trade were important to the empire. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-sikh-war">First Anglo-Sikh War</a> it was lost and transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-amritsar-1846">Treaty of Amritsar</a> of 1846.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kashmir.jpg" alt="Kashmir" width="320" height="342" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Central Intelligence Agency (old labels removed, new added by Fowler&amp;fowler 02:56, 11 April 2022 (UTC)) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kashmir_region._LOC_2003626427_-_showing_sub-regions_administered_by_different_countries.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
